wever, the process abruptly hit an `HTTP 429` error on batch processing.\n\n\n**Addressing Rate Limits**\n\nI've pinpointed the `HTTP 429` error to OpenRouter's concurrency limits. My `ThreadPoolExecutor` sent concurrent requests, exceeding the free tier's rate. The hybrid logic itself works, identifying 591 shortages swiftly. The real problem is I exceeded the rate limit. I am now considering solutions like reducing concurrency and adding delays, or simply running the requests sequentially, since it would still be *much* faster than the old LLM batch method (even if sequential). I will also re-evaluate the old LLM batch for comparison.\n\n\n**Refining Rate Limiting Strategy**\n\nI'm making progress in handling OpenRouter's rate limits. I'm focusing on refining the `coordinator.py` logic. I'm modifying the `max_workers` to be `2` (still concurrent, but less aggressive) and implementing retries with a 5-second backoff within the `process_batch` function. The prior 3-second sleep was insufficient. I'm also increasing the retry count to 5.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Reduce thread concurrency and increase backoff to prevent HTTP 429 on OpenRouter","EndLine":167,"Instruction":"Update process_batch retry logic and reduce max_workers","ReplacementContent":"            def process_batch(batch_data):\n                batch_idx, batch_cases = batch_data\n                max_retries = 6\n                for attempt in range(max_retries):\n                    try:\n                        results = self._call_openrouter({\"cases\": batch_cases})\n                        parsed = []\n                        for case, decision in zip(batch_cases, results):\n                            shortage_name = case[\"requested_name\"]\n                            status = decision.get(\"status\", \"no_match\")\n                            item_id = decision.get(\"item_id\", \"\")\n                            warehouse_item = catalog_by_id.get(item_id, \"\")\n                            \n                            parsed.append({\n                                \"shortage_name\": shortage_name,\n                                \"status\": status,\n                                \"warehouse_item\": warehouse_item\n                            })\n                        print(f\"      [✓] Batch {batch_idx+1}/{len(batches)} done.\")\n                        return parsed\n                    except Exception as e:\n                        if attempt < max_retries - 1:\n                            wait_time = 4 * (attempt + 1)\n                            print(f\"      [!] Batch {batch_idx+1} hit rate limit (429). Waiting {wait_time}s...\")\n                            time.sleep(wait_time)\n                        else:\n                            print(f\"      [!] Batch {batch_idx+1} completely failed: {e}\")\n                \n                return [{\"shortage_name\": c[\"requested_name\"], \"status\": \"no_match\", \"warehouse_item\": \"\"} for c in batch_cases]\n\n            # Reduced from 5 to 2 to prevent OpenRouter free tier 429 Rate Limits\n            with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=2) as executor:\n                results_lists = list(executor.map(process_batch, batches))","StartLine":137,"TargetContent":"            def process_batch(batch_data):\n                batch_idx, batch_cases = batch_data\n                max_retries = 3\n                for attempt in range(max_retries):\n                    try:\n                        results = self._call_openrouter({\"cases\": batch_cases})\n                        parsed = []\n                        for case, decision in zip(batch_cases, results):\n                            shortage_name = case[\"requested_name\"]\n                            status = decision.get(\"status\", \"no_match\")\n                            item_id = decision.get(\"item_id\", \"\")\n                            warehouse_item = catalog_by_id.get(item_id, \"\")\n                            \n                            parsed.append({\n                                \"shortage_name\": shortage_name,\n                                \"status\": status,\n                                \"warehouse_item\": warehouse_item\n                            })\n                        print(f\"      [✓] Batch {batch_idx+1}/{len(batches)} done.\")\n                        return parsed\n                    except Exception as e:\n                        if attempt < max_retries - 1:\n                            time.sleep(3)\n                        else:\n                            print(f\"      [!] Batch {batch_idx+1} failed: {e}\")\n                \n                return [{\"shortage_name\": c[\"requested_name\"], \"status\": \"no_match\", \"warehouse_item\": \"\"} for c in batch_cases]\n\n            with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=5) as executor:\n                results_lists = list(executor.map(process_batch, batches))","TargetFile":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\fast_match\\coordinator.py","toolAction":"Fixing HTTP 429 rate limit","toolSummary":"Fix HTTP 429"}}]}
